  "track.sysdesign.m.plan.title": "Build from the mockup, or ask first and then build",
  "track.sysdesign.m.plan.overview": "The brief: add a chat with the clinic to ClinicBook, sending text and photos. The designer sends a polished mockup. Two ways to start: code straight from the mockup; or ask the designer three questions and the backend three, then make a quick estimate of photo data before writing code.",
  "track.sysdesign.m.plan.wrapup": "A mockup only shows the best case. Errors, messy content, offline states, expired sessions, error codes and the language of notifications are all secondary requirements: if you do not ask first, they still arrive, just after release. An estimate with round numbers also reveals non-functional requirements the screen does not mention: sending original photos costs more than ten times the data of resized ones.",
  "track.sysdesign.m.plan.simp.1": "Six questions are a selection; a real session has more. Photos per day and photo sizes are illustrative assumptions, rounded the way Alex Xu advises.",
  "track.sysdesign.m.plan.simp.2": "The questions are based on Tjeerd in 't Veen ch.2; the offline and empty-state question is the site's addition. The framework and estimation follow Alex Xu vol. 1 ch.2–3.",
  "track.sysdesign.m.plan.ctl.hint": "Switch the way you start and walk again; compare the \"Requirement found\" column and the MB per month at the last step.",
